battle_controllers.c: the remake layer learns what each battler is told to do.

Every command the battle engine gives a battler's controller (a hit's blink,
a faint, a send-out, a move's animation...) passes through
PrepareBufferDataTransfer; the remake layer's hook records the battler and
the command, so the 3D body acts it out as the sprite does.

--- a/src/battle_controllers.c
+++ b/src/battle_controllers.c
@@ -1,4 +1,7 @@
 #include "global.h"
+#ifdef PLATFORM_WASM
+#include "remake_state.h"
+#endif
 #include "battle.h"
 #include "battle_ai_script_commands.h"
 #include "battle_anim.h"
@@ -656,6 +659,11 @@
